# ds4.env -- ds4-server configuration (this file IS the config surface).
#
# Seeded to /opt/data/ds4.env on first start and NEVER overwritten -- your edits
# here win. Most settings ship commented out; default values are shown in the
# commented example line and marked with "*" in a braced list. Uncomment a line
# to override it. The braced list holds supported values; hidden values are
# those which are unusable, unstable, or unhelpful on this build.
#
# ds4-server has no native per-flag environment variables, so the entrypoint
# translates the DS4_DROSTE_* settings below into command-line flags. The few
# variables the binary reads ITSELF are in their own section near the end and
# are passed through untranslated.
#
# DERIVATION RULE (flag -> variable): take the long flag, strip the leading
# "--", uppercase it, turn "-" into "_", and prefix DS4_DROSTE_ (so --kv-disk-dir
# becomes DS4_DROSTE_KV_DISK_DIR). Value flags take the value verbatim; boolean
# flags take 1/true/yes/on to enable, and empty/0/false/no/off to omit the flag.
#
# Descriptions follow "--help" at the pinned commit (kyuz0/ds4 @00e64ea, source-
# verified against ds4_server.c parse_options) with additional notes for clarity
# where practical; they are not identical to upstream documentation. Where the
# printed help and this build disagree, this file describes THIS BUILD.
#
# Reserved by droste (do not set these)
# -------------------------------------
# Droste needs these arguments to remain unchanged for its setup & teardown of
# boxes; any additions or changes are likely to break the box boot, services,
# and/or functionality.
#
#   --port      owned by PORT in /opt/data/server.env. The launcher appends it
#               and OVERWRITES any value already on the command line, so a
#               DS4_DROSTE_PORT line here would look authoritative and do
#               nothing. Change the port in server.env, then restart the box.


# Extra Arguments (options this file does not cover)
# --------------------------------------------------
# A "catch-all" setting for user-elected parameters. "Mix and match" with other
# settings may cause boot failure due to exclusions, so users should confirm
# the absence of argument conflicts in advance.
#
# Entry should be one quoted value; it is then split on whitespace into separate
# arguments, so an individual argument cannot itself contain spaces. Unused and
# tuning-only arguments are listed at the end of this file.
#
# DS4_DROSTE_EXTRA_ARGS="--warm-weights --debug"


# Model (the weights to serve)
# ----------------------------
# {absolute path}
#
# REQUIRED -- the server will not start without it. The easiest way to get one:
# run download_model.sh, which fetches a curated DeepSeek V4 quant into the
# shared HF cache and prints the absolute path to paste here. A local GGUF
# collection bind-mounted at /opt/models can be pointed at directly.
#
# Covers: --model
#
# DS4_DROSTE_MODEL=


# Backend (which compute device runs the engine)
# ----------------------------------------------
# {rocm*, cpu}
#
#   rocm    the GPU; this image is the ROCm build and defaults here
#   cpu     everything on the CPU; very slow with a large MoE quant
#
# The parser also accepts "metal", which is Apple-only and has no runtime on
# this hardware. There is NO "cuda" value: --cuda and --rocm are compile-time
# alternatives, and this image is compiled for ROCm, so ds4-server would abort
# with "unknown option" on the CUDA spelling.
#
# Covers: --backend (and the --rocm / --cpu shorthands)
#
# DS4_DROSTE_BACKEND=rocm


# Context Size (tokens the model can attend to)
# ---------------------------------------------
# {tokens}
#
# **Reasoning effort is capped below 393216. The server's own "thinking" help
# topic requires a context of at least 393216 tokens for Think Max; with a
# smaller context every request is silently capped at "high" instead. On a box
# whose reason to exist is a large quant with huge context, this is the setting
# most likely to be set once and misunderstood.
#
# Covers: --ctx
#
# DS4_DROSTE_CTX=32768 # a starting point, not the engine's own default


# Response Length (default cap on tokens generated per response)
# --------------------------------------------------------------
# {tokens}
#
# A per-request value from the API client overrides this.
#
# Covers: --tokens
#
# DS4_DROSTE_TOKENS=393216


# Prefill Chunk (prompt tokens processed per batch)
# -------------------------------------------------
# {tokens}
#
# Unset, the engine chooses. **On THIS build the automatic value is 8192 for any
# prompt longer than 4096 tokens -- not the 4096 that upstream's help text and
# README describe, which is the figure for other builds. Anyone tuning from the
# published number starts from the wrong baseline.
#
# A value of 0 is REJECTED here ("must be positive", the server exits). To
# prefill a whole prompt in one batch -- which upstream recommends when memory
# allows, and 128 GB of unified memory is that case -- leave this unset and set
# the native DS4_METAL_PREFILL_CHUNK=0 instead (see the native section).
#
# Covers: --prefill-chunk
#
# DS4_DROSTE_PREFILL_CHUNK=


# Power (percentage of available compute to use)
# ----------------------------------------------
# {1..100}
#
# Lower values trade throughput for a cooler, quieter box.
#
# Covers: --power
#
# DS4_DROSTE_POWER=100


# Speculative Decoding (MTP -- multi-token prediction)
# ----------------------------------------------------
# {path} for the draft model, {count} and {margin} to tune it
#
#   MTP         path to the optional MTP speculative-decoding GGUF
#   MTP_DRAFT   draft tokens per step. **Silently clamped to 16; the default is
#               1, and at 1 the speculative path does not run at all
#   MTP_MARGIN  acceptance margin. **Silently clamped to the range 0..1000
#
# Quality mode below applies strict MTP acceptance.
#
# Covers: --mtp, --mtp-draft, --mtp-margin
#
# DS4_DROSTE_MTP=
# DS4_DROSTE_MTP_DRAFT=1
# DS4_DROSTE_MTP_MARGIN=3.0


# Quality Mode (strict speculative acceptance)
# --------------------------------------------
# {boolean}
#
# Covers: --quality
#
# DS4_DROSTE_QUALITY=


# Warm Weights (touch all weights at load)
# ----------------------------------------
# {boolean}
#
# Pays the page-in cost up front instead of during the first requests.
#
# Covers: --warm-weights
#
# DS4_DROSTE_WARM_WEIGHTS=


# KV Cache (in memory)
# --------------------
# {tokens} for each, {boolean} for the last
#
#   KV_CACHE_MIN_TOKENS                  default 512
#   KV_CACHE_COLD_MAX_TOKENS             default 30000; 0 = unlimited
#   KV_CACHE_CONTINUED_INTERVAL_TOKENS   default 10000
#   KV_CACHE_BOUNDARY_TRIM_TOKENS        default 32
#   KV_CACHE_BOUNDARY_ALIGN_TOKENS       default 2048
#   KV_CACHE_REJECT_DIFFERENT_QUANT      boolean; ignore cache from another quant
#
# **COLD_MAX_TOKENS must be either 0 or at least MIN_TOKENS. Any other pairing
# makes the server exit at startup.
#
# Covers: --kv-cache-min-tokens, --kv-cache-cold-max-tokens,
#         --kv-cache-continued-interval-tokens, --kv-cache-boundary-trim-tokens,
#         --kv-cache-boundary-align-tokens, --kv-cache-reject-different-quant
#
# DS4_DROSTE_KV_CACHE_MIN_TOKENS=512
# DS4_DROSTE_KV_CACHE_COLD_MAX_TOKENS=30000
# DS4_DROSTE_KV_CACHE_CONTINUED_INTERVAL_TOKENS=10000
# DS4_DROSTE_KV_CACHE_BOUNDARY_TRIM_TOKENS=32
# DS4_DROSTE_KV_CACHE_BOUNDARY_ALIGN_TOKENS=2048
# DS4_DROSTE_KV_CACHE_REJECT_DIFFERENT_QUANT=


# KV Disk Cache (session cache on disk)
# -------------------------------------
# {path} and {MB}
#
# The disk cache is CACHE class: it lives on the box's program-cache volume
# (/opt/program-cache), which the installer may empty on your say-so. Saved
# sessions (~/.ds4, i.e. /opt/data/internal) are NOT in that wipe. Re-point the
# directory at a path under /opt/data only if you want the KV cache backed up
# with your data.
#
# Covers: --kv-disk-dir, --kv-disk-space-mb
#
DS4_DROSTE_KV_DISK_DIR=/opt/program-cache/kv-disk
# DS4_DROSTE_KV_DISK_SPACE_MB=4096


# Tool Calling & Reasoning Replay
# -------------------------------
# {count} and {boolean}
#
#   TOOL_MEMORY_MAX_IDS                 tool-call ids retained per session
#   DISABLE_EXACT_DSML_TOOL_REPLAY      boolean; turn off exact tool replay
#
# Covers: --tool-memory-max-ids, --disable-exact-dsml-tool-replay
#
# DS4_DROSTE_TOOL_MEMORY_MAX_IDS=100000
# DS4_DROSTE_DISABLE_EXACT_DSML_TOOL_REPLAY=


# Server API (how the HTTP surface behaves)
# -----------------------------------------
# {address}, {boolean}, {path}
#
#   HOST    ds4-server's own default is 127.0.0.1; droste sets 0.0.0.0 so the
#           box is reachable from the host and the LAN. **There is no
#           authentication and no TLS on this port -- anything that can route
#           to the box can use the model. Set 127.0.0.1 to restrict it to
#           in-box clients.
#   CORS    boolean; enable CORS headers for browser clients
#   TRACE   path; write a request trace file
#
# Covers: --host, --cors, --trace
#
DS4_DROSTE_HOST=0.0.0.0
# DS4_DROSTE_CORS=
# DS4_DROSTE_TRACE=


# Directional Steering (activation steering at inference)
# -------------------------------------------------------
# {path} and two {-100..100} scales
#
# **The FILE is required for the scales. Setting FFN or ATTN without a steering
# file is FATAL, not ignored: the engine refuses to open and the server exits.
# A file with no scale is fine -- FFN then defaults to 1.0.
#
# Covers: --dir-steering-file, --dir-steering-ffn, --dir-steering-attn
#
# DS4_DROSTE_DIR_STEERING_FILE=
# DS4_DROSTE_DIR_STEERING_FFN=
# DS4_DROSTE_DIR_STEERING_ATTN=


# Working Directory (chdir before serving)
# ----------------------------------------
# {path}
#
# Parsed by the server but not printed in its help; it is fully documented for
# ds4-agent and the server arm is identical.
#
# Covers: --chdir
#
# DS4_DROSTE_CHDIR=


# Memory Simulation (pretend some memory is already in use)
# ---------------------------------------------------------
# {GiB value, e.g. 64GB}
#
# For rehearsing behaviour on a smaller machine.
#
# Covers: --simulate-used-memory
#
# DS4_DROSTE_SIMULATE_USED_MEMORY=


# Native ds4 variables (read by the binary itself, not translated)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# These are passed through untouched. ds4-server reads 168 DS4_* variables in
# total; upstream documents exactly one of them, and the rest read as internal
# tuning and diagnostics. The handful that matter on this box:
#
#   DS4_THREADS
#     Engine thread count -- the native form of --threads, which is why there is
#     no DS4_DROSTE_THREADS. (A --threads flag would win over this variable, and
#     droste never emits one.)
#
#   DS4_LOCK_FILE
#     **A RUNNING SERVER LOCKS OUT EVERY OTHER ds4 TOOL IN THE BOX. The engine
#     takes an exclusive lock on /tmp/ds4.lock, and ds4, ds4-agent, ds4-bench
#     and ds4-eval all take the same one -- the second process exits with
#     "another ds4 process is already running". Pointing a second process at a
#     different lock file is the only way to run the CLI against your quant
#     while the server is up. Documented by nobody upstream.
#
#   DS4_METAL_PREFILL_CHUNK
#     The one variable upstream's README documents. **The _METAL_ in the name is
#     historical -- the ROCm runtime reads it. It is consulted ONLY when
#     --prefill-chunk is unset, and 0 means "prefill the whole prompt in one
#     batch", a mode the flag cannot express because it rejects 0.
#
#   DS4_SERVER_DISABLE_THINK_TOOL_RECOVERY
#     Turns off the think-tool recovery path.
#
#   DS4_MTP_SPEC_DISABLE
#     **Conditional, not absolute: the branch it guards runs only when MTP draft
#     tokens are above 1 and sampling is greedy. At stock settings the
#     speculative path never runs and this variable does nothing. It becomes
#     live once DS4_DROSTE_MTP_DRAFT is raised.
#
# DS4_THREADS=
# DS4_LOCK_FILE=
# DS4_METAL_PREFILL_CHUNK=
# DS4_SERVER_DISABLE_THINK_TOOL_RECOVERY=1
# DS4_MTP_SPEC_DISABLE=1


# Options for Debugging & Development
# -----------------------------------
# Diagnostic
#   --debug (coordinator route/debug logs), --help <topic> (runtime,
#   distributed, steering, api, kv-cache, thinking, all)
#
# Native
#   DS4_METAL_GRAPH_DUMP_PREFIX (compute-graph dumps; read by the ROCm runtime
#   despite the name)


# Unused Arguments (inapplicable / unsupported in this build)
# -----------------------------------------------------------
# SSD expert streaming -- **METAL ONLY; FATAL HERE
#   --ssd-streaming, --ssd-streaming-cold, --ssd-streaming-cache-experts,
#   --ssd-streaming-preload-experts
#
#   Upstream's own help begins these with "Metal SSD streaming". On any other
#   backend the engine prints "--ssd-streaming is currently supported only with
#   --metal" and the server EXITS -- after the model has been opened. The three
#   companion flags feed only that path, so they are silent no-ops alone and a
#   dead box alongside it. On a machine bought to run an 80-430 GB quant,
#   "stream experts from SSD" is the most tempting line upstream prints, which
#   is why it is named here rather than left to be discovered.
#
#   These have no setting. The entrypoint additionally REFUSES to pass them to a
#   non-Metal backend, warning instead, so an older ds4.env that still sets them
#   will start rather than die -- but do not rely on that to hide a typo.
#
# Distributed serving (out of single-box scope)
#   --role, --layers, --listen, --coordinator, --dist-prefill-chunk,
#   --dist-prefill-window, --dist-activation-bits, --dist-replay-check
#
# Backend shorthands (redundant with DS4_DROSTE_BACKEND)
#   --metal (Apple hardware only), --rocm, --cpu
